eSPX agent rules index

**Client docs:** `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/SELF_HOSTED.md`, `docs/PROTECTION.md`, `docs/LICENSE_COMMERCE.md`, `docs/TELEMETRY_AND_TRUST.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`, `docs/runbooks/`.

**Agent design:** `.cursor/MULTI_REGION.md`, `.cursor/COMPLIANCE_MATRIX.md`.

**Open work:** `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` (deferred gaps + completed roadmap). Milestone stub: `docs/MILESTONE.md`.

**Agent rules:** `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — scoped by glob; start here.

- `espx.mdc` — SLA, layout, hot-path summary (always)
- `code-style.mdc` — Go, Lua, SQL, Python structure and PR gates
- `hot-path.mdc` — `internal/ingestion`, tracker ingest
- `cold-path.mdc` — notify, payment, ledger, costsync, controlplane, admin (no GoF/SOLID)
- `load-test-bpf.mdc` — BPF + Prometheus perf validation
- `data-layer.mdc` — Redis, Postgres, ClickHouse
- `control-plane.mdc` — management, outbox, admin APIs
- `rtb.mdc` — in-process auction, OpenRTB
- `edge.mdc` — nginx Lua, XDP
- `compliance.mdc` — defensive perimeter
- `fault-resilience.mdc` — fault injection tests
- `service-boundaries.mdc` — `cmd/*` imports
- `open-gaps.mdc` — routes to `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`
- `capabilities.mdc` — client vs agent doc routing

**Precedence:** `espx.mdc` on `/track` SLA and allocs; `hot-path.mdc` on ingestion; `cold-path.mdc` on notify/payment/ledger/costsync/controlplane (bans Provider/Factory/mock layers); `code-style.mdc` on structure; `service-boundaries.mdc` on imports; `load-test-bpf.mdc` before perf claims.

Do not duplicate agent rules into `docs/` — maintain `.cursor/rules/` only.
